# third_party/swisseph — vendored Swiss Ephemeris (Phase-2 engine)

See VERSION for the upstream pin (tag, commit, anchor hash) and the
vendored file list. Rationale for vendoring instead of fetching at
build time: byte-stable source for a fidelity-critical project, zero
new build tooling (no vcpkg/Conan yet), offline builds keep working.

Rules:
- NEVER hand-edit the vendored files. Upstream updates arrive as a
  new VERSION pin + fresh copies (record the new anchor hash).
- The `swisseph` CMake target compiles with warnings suppressed
  (`-w`); our `-Wall -Wextra` zero-warning gate applies to our
  code only.
- Moshier fallback only (no `*.se1` data). If data files are ever
  added, document where they come from and how L1 bounds change.
